text:
MCP ServerAccess MrScraper’s web scraping API via a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server to enable AI agents to fetch and extract web data securely.Use MrScraper’s web scraping API through the Model Context Protocol (MCP) to let AI agents discover, fetch, and extract web data in real time. This cloud-hosted MCP server integrates directly with MrScraper, enabling secure, scalable scraping workflows without local setup or infrastructure management.

AI ScrapingExtract structured data using natural language instructions powered by AI.Geo UnblockerAccess geo-restricted and protected websites with built-in unblocker support.Scraper ExecutionRun scrapers manually or trigger AI-driven executions based on your workflow.Bulk ScrapingPerform large-scale scraping operations across multiple URLs in one run.Results ManagementRetrieve, organize, and manage scraping results from a centralized interface.Rotating ProxiesImprove reliability with rotating residential proxy support.Cloud MCP ServerUse a fully managed, cloud-hosted MCP server with no local installation required.

To use the MrScraper MCP server, you'll need:

A MrScraper account
MrScraper API Token

The simplest way to use MrScraper MCP is through our remotely hosted server. No local installation required!
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "mrscraper": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.mrscraper.com/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer <MRSCRAPER_API_TOKEN>"
      }
    }
  }
}
NoteThis configuration uses the HTTP transport protocol to connect to our hosted
MCP server at https://mcp.mrscraper.com/mcp and authenticates with the
Authorization header.

Find your config file.OSPathmacOS~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.jsonWindows%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.jsonYou can also open it from inside Claude Desktop via Settings → Developer → Edit Config.Add this to your Claude config file (claude_desktop_config.json)::{
  "mcpServers": {
    "mrscraper": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "mcp-remote@latest",
        "https://mcp.mrscraper.com/mcp",
        "--header",
        "Authorization: Bearer <MRSCRAPER_API_TOKEN>"
      ]
    }
  }
}Save the file and fully restart Claude Desktop. You should see a 🔨 hammer icon in the chat input box, indicating MCP tools are active.

Add the MrScraper MCP server using the Claude Code CLI:
claude mcp add mrscraper --transport http https://mcp.mrscraper.com/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer <MRSCRAPER_API_TOKEN>"

NoteRequires Cursor version 0.45.6+.
