        "Authorization": "Bearer <MRSCRAPER_API_TOKEN>"
      }
    }
  }
}

Google Antigravity allows you to configure MCP servers directly through its Agent interface.
Open the MCP store via the ... dropdown at the top of the editor's agent panelClick on Manage MCP ServersModify the mcp_config.json with your custom MCP server configurationAdd the following configuration:{
  "mcpServers": {
    "mrscraper": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.mrscraper.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}Save the file and click Refresh in the Antigravity MCP interface.

To connect the MrScraper MCP server in n8n:
In your n8n workflow, add an AI Agent node.In the AI Agent configuration, add a new Tool.Select MCP Client Tool as the tool type.Enter the MCP server Endpoint:https://mcp.mrscraper.com/mcpSet Server Transport to HTTP Streamable.Set Authentication to None (authentication is handled via MCP headers).For Tools to include, you can select All, Selected, or All Except.

The MrScraper MCP server provides comprehensive scraping tools.

Creates an AI-powered scraper that intelligently extracts structured data from a website.

{
  "url": "https://example.com/page",
  "message": "Extract product names and prices",
  "agent": "general",
  "proxy_country": "US"
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionurlYesTarget URL to scrape.messageYesNatural language instructions for data extraction.agentNoScraper agent type: general (default), listing, or map.proxy_countryNoISO country code for proxy routing (e.g., US, GB).

{
  "url": "https://example.com/page",
  "agent": "map",
  "max_depth": 2,
  "max_pages": 50,
  "limit": 1000,
  "include_patterns": "",
  "exclude_patterns": ""
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionurlYesTarget URL to scrape.agentYesThe map agent type.max_depthNoMaximum crawl depth (default: 2).max_pagesNoMaximum number of pages to scrape (default: 50).limitNoMaximum number of records to extract (default: 1000).include_patternsNoURL patterns to include (regex).exclude_patternsNoURL patterns to exclude (regex).

Reruns an existing AI-powered scraper on a new URL with crawling parameters.
{
  "scraper_id": "scraper_12345",
  "url": "https://example.com/category",
  "max_depth": 2,
  "max_pages": 50,
  "limit": 1000,
  "include_patterns": "*/products/*",
  "exclude_patterns": "*/cart/*||*/checkout/*"
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionscraper_idYesAI Scraper ID returned from create_scraper.urlYesTarget URL to scrape.max_depthNoMaximum crawl depth (default: 2).max_pagesNoMaximum number of pages to scrape (default: 50).limitNoMaximum number of records to extract (default: 1000).include_patternsNoURL patterns to include (regex).exclude_patternsNoURL patterns to exclude (regex).

Reruns an existing AI scraper on multiple URLs simultaneously in one batch.
{
  "scraper_id": "scraper_12345",
  "urls": [
    "https://example.com/page1",
    "https://example.com/page2",
    "https://example.com/page3"
  ]
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionscraper_idYesAI scraper ID (configured via web dashboard).urlYesTarget URL to scrape.

Reruns a manually configured scraper (with custom selectors/rules) on a new URL.
{
  "scraper_id": "manual_scraper_67890",
  "url": "https://example.com/new-item"
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionscraper_idYesManual scraper ID (configured via web dashboard).urlYesTarget URL to scrape.

Reruns an existing manual scraper on multiple URLs simultaneously in one batch.
{
  "scraper_id": "scraper_12345",
  "urls": [
    "https://example.com/page1",
    "https://example.com/page2",
    "https://example.com/page3"
  ]
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionscraper_idYesManual scraper ID (configured via web dashboard).urlYesTarget URL to scrape.

Fetches HTML content from a URL with stealth, unblocking, and rendering capabilities.
{
  "url": "https://example.com/page",
  "timeout": 120,
  "geo_code": "US",
  "block_resources": false
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionurlYesTarget URL to fetch.timeoutNoMaximum wait time in seconds (default: 120).geo_codeNoISO country code for geolocation (default: US).block_resourcesNoWhether to block images, CSS, and fonts (default: false).

Retrieves a paginated list of all scraping results with filtering, sorting, and search.
{
  "sort_field": "updatedAt",
  "sort_order": "DESC",
  "page_size": 10,
  "page": 1,
  "search": "product",
  "date_range_column": "updatedAt",
  "start_at": "2024-01-01",
  "end_at": "2024-01-08"
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionsort_fieldNoSort field (createdAt, updatedAt, id, type, url, status, etc.).sort_orderNoSort order: ASC or DESC (default: DESC).page_sizeNoNumber of results per page (default: 10).pageNoPage number (default: 1).searchNoFree-text search query.date_range_columnNoDate field for filtering (updatedAt, createdAt, scrapedAt).start_atNoStart date (ISO 8601: YYYY-MM-DD).end_atNoEnd date (ISO 8601: YYYY-MM-DD).

Retrieves detailed information for a specific scraping result by its result ID.
{
  "result_id": "result_12345"
}

ParameterRequiredDescriptionresult_idYesUnique identifier of the scraping result.

The MrScraper MCP server provides comprehensive error handling:

401 Unauthorized: Invalid or missing Authorization header.
500 Internal Server Error: Internal/Unexpected server error (Contact support@mrscraper.com if the issue persistent).

Example error response:
{
  "error": "Unauthorized or invalid credentials. Please go to https://app.mrscraper.com to get your API token.",
  "status_code": 401
}
